{title: From the Mouths of Children}
{subtitle: Psalms 8:2–3}
{key: C}
{tempo: 102}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [G] | [Am] |
| [F] [G] | [C] | [G] | [F] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]When I look up [G/B]at the [Am]sky
The [F]moon and [C/E]stars you [G]made
[C]What are we [G/B]that you think of [Am]us
And [F]care for [C/G]us [G]each [C]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G/B]Lord, our [Am]Lord, how ma[F]jestic is your [G]name
In all the [Am]earth, in all the [F]earth
From the [G]mouths of children [Am]you [G]made [F]strength
Lord, our [G]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Every little [G]voice can [Am]sing
And [F]every [C/E]child can [G]pray
You set your [Am]splendor [Em]in the [F]heavens
[C/E]And hear the [Dm7]songs [G]we [C]raise
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [C] | [G] | [F] | [G] |
